<p>Eileen Wang, the mayor of Arcadia, California, resigned Monday after the U.S. Justice Department charged her with acting in the United States as an illegal agent of the Chinese government and said she agreed to plead guilty to the felony count. The charge carries a maximum sentence of 10 years in federal prison, and Fox News reported that Wang also faces a potential $250,000 fine, with sentencing to be determined by a federal judge. Prosecutors said Wang acted at the direction and control of Chinese government officials from at least 2020 through 2022, coordinating with people in the United States to promote Beijing’s interests without notifying the U.S. attorney general as required by law. The Justice Department said Wang and Yaoning “Mike” Sun used the U.S. News Center, a website presented as a news source for Southern California’s Chinese American community, to publish pro-China material. Court documents described a June 2021 episode in which Chinese government officials sent Wang prewritten material over WeChat, including an essay denying genocide and forced labor in Xinjiang; prosecutors said Wang posted it on her website within minutes and returned the link to the group chat. Sun has pleaded guilty in a related case and is serving a four-year prison sentence.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4n4Guuacmo6e34q7ernz51Ql9NoLOgqeyTAbJCdcVinbDlBeRa7OgDLg0CBuJsqJv-STnbOCrUDUNI8u-_teRpPRjGWJIll_zIWyurq7JVhji05ISzBs1BcfSsmQA-qcGsbTdh1gZInNB6AhbBfZ-NNlyqtTXsoUPwHmoKXO6-YIy3qr3DjfAujzgLyiwhGpG3KLF7x-fLHLX3eu8YIjB-bjtKHdOp-n1YMzk460pSViv06DYuLZADnr7zIVTAbfaGzwOj50Z66JHq6En68e' alt='Eileen Wang, the Arcadia, California mayor who resigned after agreeing to plead guilty to acting as an illegal agent of China.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Readership tracking: Prosecutors said Wang sent screenshots to Chinese officials to show article page views, including evidence that one item had topped 10,000 views.</li><li>WeChat messages: In the Xinjiang-related exchange, a Chinese official replied, “So fast, thank you everyone,” after Wang and others posted links, according to prosecutors cited by KRON4.</li><li>Court schedule: SFist, citing the Los Angeles Times, said Wang was scheduled to be arraigned Tuesday.</li><li>Past denial: CNA said Wang denied the allegations to the Los Angeles Times in May 2025.</li></ul><blockquote>Individuals elected to public office in the United States should act only for the people of the United States that they represent - John A. Eisenberg</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Justice Department: Assistant Attorney General for National Security John A. Eisenberg said the case was deeply concerning because prosecutors allege Wang carried out directives from Chinese government officials and later held a position of public trust. (<a href='https://www.foxnews.com/us/california-mayor-accused-secretly-working-china-spreading-propaganda-office-feds'>Fox News</a>)</li><li>Arcadia city officials: City officials said the case related to Wang’s individual conduct and did not affect municipal operations. (<a href='https://www.foxnews.com/us/california-mayor-accused-secretly-working-china-spreading-propaganda-office-feds'>Fox News</a>)</li><li>Federal investigators: The FBI said people who try to influence U.S. democratic institutions for a foreign government must be identified and held accountable under the law. (<a href='https://www.seoul.co.kr/news/newsView.php?id=20260512500148'>Seoul Shinmun</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3353203/southern-california-mayor-will-plead-guilty-acting-agent-chinese-government'>California mayor resigns, will plead guilty to acting as a China agent</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-la-area-mayor-to-plead-guilty-to-acting-as-chinese-agent/a-77126713'>US: LA area mayor to plead guilty to acting as Chinese agent</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2